flowchart TB
  accTitle: Remote Python Debugging Through an SSH Tunnel
  accDescr: The local editor connects to localhost:5678, forwarded through SSH to debugpy listening on the server's port 5678. When the Python program pauses at a breakpoint, the editor can inspect variables and the call stack and control stepping.
  subgraph local["Local computer"]
    direction TB
    editor["VSCode / Cursor / Windsurf<br/>Python: Remote Attach"]
    controls["Set breakpoints · Step through code<br/>Inspect variables · View the call stack"]
    endpoint["Local connection endpoint<br/>localhost:5678"]
    controls <--> editor
    editor <--> endpoint
  end
  tunnel["SSH tunnel<br/>LocalForward 5678 localhost:5678"]
  subgraph remote["Remote server"]
    direction TB
    debugpy["debugpy<br/>Listen on server port 5678"]
    program["Python program<br/>For example, train.py"]
    paused["Pause at a breakpoint<br/>Inspect the current runtime state"]
    debugpy <--> program
    program --> paused
  end
  local <-->|"Debug requests and state"| tunnel
  tunnel <--> remote
